{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And between the altar.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, wrote: this is the altar of burnt offering, which stands before the entrance of the Tent of Meeting. And the laver was drawn slightly forward and stood opposite the space between the altar and the Tabernacle, and it did not interpose between them at all — because it is said (Exodus 40:6): ״ונתת את מזבח העולה לפני פתח משכן אהל מועד״ — 'the altar before the Tent of Meeting,' and not the laver before the Tent of Meeting. How so? It was drawn slightly toward the south. Thus is it taught in Zevahim, end of quote. And this laver was like a large basin that has twelve spouts through which water was poured, corresponding to the twelve priests occupied with the daily offering who sanctify their hands and feet simultaneously. And even though the priests occupied with the daily offering were thirteen, and thirteen labors were taught in the Mishnah, the slaughter does not require a priest, since it is valid through a non-priest (zar) and does not require sanctification of hands and feet even for a priest."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:39.675692110Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}